From 833720c23f0ae6ada43cbfea2ac80db9db30138b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefane Fermigier <sf@abilian.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:23:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 111/142] OdfFile writer: booleans as true/false, unset
 optionals left out

Streaming a C++ bool into an attribute writes 0 or 1, and ODF's
boolean type allows only true and false. Fixed where the writer does
that: text:h (restart-numbering, is-list-header), table column and row
groups (table:display), and line numbering (text:number-lines).
Boolean spreadsheet cells had the same fault by another route: the
XLSX cell text, 0 or 1, was copied into office:boolean-value.

Streaming an unset boost::optional writes "--". Every optional
attribute of the data pilot elements was written that way, so a
data-pilot-table without, say, a grand-total came out with
table:grand-total="--". They now use CP_XML_ATTR_OPT like the rest
of the writer.

Across LibreOffice's 3794 ODF test documents these account for 531
documents with bad boolean cells, 39 with "--" attributes, and 15
with bad heading attributes.

OdfFile writer: collapsed outline groups say so

The writer never set table:display on a column or row group, so every
group came out displayed. Writing that bool as 1 used to hide this:
the reader does not take 1 for true, so on the next trip every group
read as collapsed, and hidden columns stayed hidden by accident. With
the value now a valid true, the next trip believes it and the hidden
columns come back visible (sc/qa/unit/data/ods/outline.ods).

XLSX says a group is collapsed only by hiding its members, so the
table state now counts each group's members and hidden members, and a
group whose members are all hidden is written table:display=false.
One hidden row in an open group does not collapse it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
